00:19:12.310 --> 00:19:17.710
From the moment a Plains Indian child was born and wrapped in a soft layer of buffalo

00:19:17.710 --> 00:19:25.240
hair and a tanned calfskin, to the time his or her corpse was shrouded in a bison robe,

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:28.290
every day of life was connected with the buffalo.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:36.100
In winter, when the bison's fur was the thickest, its hide would be tanned and turned into a

00:19:36.100 --> 00:19:43.390
warm robe. In the summer, when the hides had less hair, they could be sewn together into

00:19:43.390 --> 00:19:51.560
coverings for teepees. Stretched over a frame of curved willow branches, a hide was transformed

00:19:51.560 --> 00:20:00.000
into a bowl-like boat for crossing rivers. A buffalo's bladder became a water container. Its shoulder blade

00:20:00.000 --> 00:20:09.170
a digging tool, its horn a spoon or a cup. Buffalo teeth became ornaments. Some women

00:20:09.170 --> 00:20:13.680
